course: dictionary
lesson: 12723
title: Drab: dull and grey
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Drab is an adjective. It means dull and plain, with no bright colours or interest. Read the words around it to find its meaning: «The walls of the old room were drab and grey, with no pictures and no colour.» The clues are grey and no colour, so drab must mean dull and plain.
explain: Drab can also describe a place or a life with no fun or excitement. «The town felt drab after the fair packed up and left.» The fair has gone, so the town is boring. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Drab is not the same as sad. Sad describes a feeling, but drab describes how something looks or feels. A brown coat can be drab, and a grey, boring day can be drab too.
fact: Drab is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a drab room, drab clothes, a drab town.
fact: Drab means dull and boring, with no bright colours or interest.
fact: «Drab and grey» is a common pair of words, as in «a drab and grey winter sky».
fact: Some female birds have drab brown feathers so they can hide from enemies while they sit on the nest.
exercise: «The walls of the old room were drab and grey.» What does drab mean here? | Very tall | Full of music and noise | Bright and sparkly | *Dull and plain, with no bright colours
exercise: Mia says drab means colourful. Is she right? | Yes, because it sounds like crab | No, it means very tall | Yes, drab means full of bright colours | *No, drab means dull, with no bright colours
exercise: Which word best fits? «The party was fun, but the waiting room was ___ and boring.» | tasty | *drab | bright | loud
test: «The farm was drab in the winter rain, with grey fields and no flowers.» What does drab mean here? | Noisy and crowded | Tasty and sweet | *Dull and plain | Bright and busy
test: Why are some female birds drab? | To be seen by everyone from far away | To shine brightly in the sun | *To hide from enemies while they sit on the nest | To sing louder than the males
exam: Read: «The drab little room had no colour and no fun.» Which word is closest in meaning to drab? | *Dull | Noisy | Bright | Cheerful
